findings.fix:
In variables.tf, add:

variable "max_instance_count" {
  type        = number
  default     = null
  description = "Maximum number of container instances Cloud Run may scale to; null uses the project default (currently unbounded from this module's perspective)"

  validation {
    condition     = var.max_instance_count == null || var.max_instance_count > 0
    error_message = "max_instance_count must be a positive number or null"
  }
}

In google_cloud_run_v2_service.tf, inside the template block (after encryption_key, before the vpc_access dynamic block):

    dynamic "scaling" {
      for_each = var.max_instance_count != null ? [1] : []
      content {
        max_instance_count = var.max_instance_count
      }
    }

In variables.tf, add:

variable "min_instance_count" {
  type        = number
  default     = null
  description = "Minimum number of container instances to keep warm; null allows scale-to-zero (default Cloud Run behavior)"

  validation {
    condition     = var.min_instance_count == null || var.min_instance_count >= 0
    error_message = "min_instance_count must be a non-negative number or null"
  }
}

Extend the scaling dynamic block from HOLDEN_BP_002's fix to include both:

    dynamic "scaling" {
      for_each = var.max_instance_count != null || var.min_instance_count != null ? [1] : []
      content {
        min_instance_count = var.min_instance_count
        max_instance_count = var.max_instance_count
      }
    }
